{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSXDVdUkpwDM1J31BD8S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me summarize my analysis findings:\n\n**REQUIREMENT, RESTATED:**\nAdd a POST endpoint `/shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` that transitions a shipment from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipments, rejects CANCELLED shipments with HTTP 409, and returns 404 for non-existent shipments.\n\n**REPOSITORY FINDINGS:**\n- Shipment entity at `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9` with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController at `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20` - existing endpoints: create, getById, list\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11` with save(), findById()\n- ShipmentControllerTest at `src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23` - existing 5 tests, all passing\n- Error handling uses ApiException subclasses: ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- ErrorCode enum at `src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31` defines machine-readable error codes\n\n**CONVENTIONS THIS REPOSITORY HAS:**\n- Endpoints use Spring annotations (@PostMapping, @GetMapping, @PathVariable, @RequestBody)\n- Error handling throws ApiException subclasses rather than building error bodies\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions, checking $.error.code for error codes\n- POST endpoints return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...) for creation\n- Controllers inject repositories via constructor\n- Endpoints retrieve by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException with error code and message\n\n**AFFECTED FILES:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - add ErrorCode for invalid shipment state during confirm\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - add tests for confirm endpoint (4 cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent, CANCELLED rejection, 404)\n\n**RISKS:**\n- Breaking existing 13 tests if I modify Shipment structure or repository\n- ErrorCode enum is described as public API (clients switch on it), so new code is intentional change\n- Idempotent behavior requires handling CONFIRMED status without error\n\n**OPEN QUESTIONS:**\n- None; the requirement is clear on all four cases\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**PROPOSED CHANGE:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add new ErrorCode enum value `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` to signal when attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment (409 Conflict makes sense because the shipment is in an incompatible state).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add new endpoint:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Retrieve shipment by ID, throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\n   - If status is CREATED, transition to CONFIRMED and save\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent, return unchanged)\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) with the current/updated shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four tests:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` - POST to confirm, verify status changed\n   - `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment` - create, confirm, confirm again, verify succeeds\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` - write CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, POST confirm, verify 409 and error code\n   - `returns 404 when confirming unknown shipment` - POST confirm for non-existent ID, verify 404 and error code\n\n**ALTERNATIVE REJECTED:**\n- **Create a Service layer**: The ticket says \"Do not modify files outside the shipment feature, except tests if required.\" Adding a ShipmentService would be unnecessary since the logic is simple state transitions; the controller can handle it inline like create() does.\n- **New status like IN_TRANSIT**: The ticket defines exactly three statuses (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED) and requires confirm to move CREATED→CONFIRMED only.\n- **Return 400 for CANCELLED**: The ticket explicitly says 409, which is correct semantically (conflict with current state).\n\n**DATA AND ERROR FLOW:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Status | Response |\n|------|------|-------|--------|----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | repository.findById(shipmentId) | repository.save(Shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 OK | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | repository.findById(shipmentId) | none | 200 OK | Shipment unchanged |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | repository.findById(shipmentId) | none | 409 | error.code=SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM |\n| Confirm unknown ID | repository.findById returns null | none | 404 | error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**TEST STRATEGY:**\n\n1. **Test: confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED**\n   - Create shipment via POST /shipments\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Assert status 200 OK\n   - Assert response $.status = \"CONFIRMED\"\n\n2. **Test: confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment**\n   - Create and confirm shipment\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm again\n   - Assert status 200 OK (does not fail)\n   - Assert response $.status = \"CONFIRMED\" (unchanged)\n\n3. **Test: rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409**\n   - Directly insert CANCELLED shipment in repository\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Assert status 409 Conflict\n   - Assert $.error.code = \"SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM\"\n\n4. **Test: returns 404 when confirming unknown shipment**\n   - POST /shipments/unknown-id/confirm\n   - Assert status 404 Not Found\n   - Assert $.error.code = \"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\"\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"c